# `=` in a `where` predicate: DS0110, with a fix to `==`. The tree reads it as a comparison.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | where customerId = "c-001"
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..42
  PIPELINE@0..41
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..41
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      BIN_EXPR@21..41
        NAME_REF@21..31
          IDENT@21..31 "customerId"
        WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
        EQ@32..33 "="
        WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
        LITERAL@34..41
          STRING@34..41 "\"c-001\""
  WHITESPACE@41..42 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `=` is assignment, not comparison
  --> query:1:33
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | where customerId = "c-001"
  |                                 ^ assignment is not allowed here
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `customerId == "c-001"`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | where customerId == "c-001"
which parses without errors
